ils \u2014 not a marginal miss.\n- **step_04** (confounder control): Static 2-hop neighbourhood around 1006 is dense via hubs 45, 153, 1680, so static reachability is abundant yet temporally unusable.\n- **step_12** (confounder control): The gatekeepers into 1860 (153: 162 events/134 partners; 182: 68 events) and out of 1006 (1680: 72 events; 45: 61) are high-degree hubs \u2014 popularity, not cascade timing. **step_10/step_11** show neither 153 nor 182 is even reachable from 1006 under \u0394\u2264600, so the final hop into 1860 can never be primed.\n- **step_05**: Both endpoints are sparse (5 events each), so the apparent link is carried entirely by hub volume (step_02: 7200 events).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_30df0d06\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860],\n  \"window\": [18031, 56431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.91,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No \u0394\u2264600 time-respecting cascade runs from 1006 to 1860 in [18031,56431]. The constrained forward cone from 1006 covers just 8 nodes and excludes 1860, and path enumeration returns nothing. The pair is connected only when waiting is unbounded: the earliest-arrival route needs gaps up to 9109 units (median gap ~2000), i.e. relay nodes acted days apart rather than in a chain of prompt responses. Relaxing the threshold to